Z||000000||Seanh||07-22-2001||09:54 PM||||I have a simple question. I replaced the pickup on an engine today, because at times the fuel pump (new also) would not start when the engine was cranked. Drove the car, shut it off, and it happened again. So, since the pickup plugs into the mod., could the mod. be causing the problems? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||07-22-2001||09:59 PM||||Yup, module can do it too.<P>Oh, you're talking about the module messing with the fuel pump. I don't think so, but am not sure. I know the module works with the injectors, but don't think the pump is in anyway controlled by the module.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 07-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||07-22-2001||10:40 PM||||I had the exact same problem with a fairly new module that came with the rebuilt NAPA distributor I installed late spring.  The car would often not start when hot.  It felt like it wasn't getting any fuel.  <P>Determined that I wasn't getting any spark when it wouldn't start.  Problem turned out to be the module.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
